ne, so count is 0. || EQUIPMENT not stored as rows: energy pistol and energy rifle of choice (usually heavy types; Triax allowed); bedroll and uniforms have no catalog row. The silver plated survival knife (2D4 S.D.C.) is stored as the catalog''s Knife, Silver Plated. The armor line is Standard Red Star body armor or cyborg body armor; only the Red Star suit is stored. || CYBERNETICS not stored: the block prints percentages of who is a cyborg, a numbered list of common military features and a combat systems list (first three standard, then 1D4+1 optional systems of choice); none is a fixed grant to every soldier, so all of it is in GM Notes. Catalog rows that match items on those lists: universal-headjack-and-ear-implant, cyberlink-vehicle-interfacing, gromeko-friend-or-foe-identification-computer, light-filters-cyber-optic, cyborg-helmet-and-face-plate, rvb-31-concealed-vibro-blade, pl-31-palm-laser-torch, tool-hand, shoulder-weapon-mounts-clamps, cyborg-jet-pack. || OFFICER: the typical Soviet Officer paragraph (four MOS skills at +15%, five other skills instead of three, Hand to Hand: Martial Arts or Assassin if anarchist or evil) is in GM Notes and is not a separate class or variant here."
