## Lore

The Sovietski soldier serves the Red Army of New Moscow, the one power in
Russia that still runs something like a nation. Where the police keep order
inside the cities, the Army guards the borders, the factories and the bases,
turns back Warlord raids and fights open war when it comes.

Much of that war is against the supernatural: gargoyle and Brodkil hordes,
demons, ghouls, vampires, witches and necromancers. Soldiers carry silver and
a cross as standard issue alongside their energy weapons.

The Army leans heavily on bionics. About half its soldiers are partial
cyborgs or full conversion Machines, and most of the rest carry a few
implants or a bionic limb. Their armor is black with red metallic plating and
a silver star.

## GM Notes

The block prints no Money line and no salary; starting money is the GM''s call.

MOS: three skills at +15% each, from any skill categories at all, whether or
not the category is normally available to the class.

Starting kit beyond what the sheet lists: an energy pistol and an energy rifle
of choice (usually heavy types, Triax included), a bedroll and uniforms. A
Light Machine or other ''Borg gets cyborg body armor in place of the Red Star
suit, plus the ammunition and equipment suited to the cyborg body and its
weapon systems, with regular maintenance and repairs.

Vehicle: none to start. On assignment: additional equipment, weapons,
explosives, heavy armor, jet pack or other military vehicles, plus access to
military bases (low security clearance), military doctors, hospitals and
other facilities, all depending on the local commander, supply, location and
combat conditions.

Typical bionics: 20% are 55% conversion partial cyborgs, 15% are 70-80%
conversion partial ''Borgs, 15% are full conversion Light or Heavy Machines,
and about 50% are completely human with 1D4 implants and/or one bionic limb.

Common military features: full 20/20 enhanced color vision; targeting sight
(+1 to strike) and light filters; telescopic eye with passive nightvision
(5000 ft); universal headjack/ear implant with augmentation; amplified audio;
built-in radio transmitter and receiver (5 miles); two cyberlink vehicle
interfaces (hand and head); Gromeko Friend or Foe Identification Computer;
bionic lung with gas filter and oxygen storage cell; bionic running speed of
120 mph; leaping 12 feet high or 18 feet long, half again as far with a
running start. 70% have an attractive, human face.

Combat systems: one forearm weapon on each arm (typically laser or ion), two
hand weapons of choice or a concealed Vibro-Blade, and a helmet and face
plate, plus 1D4+1 optional systems of choice from: wrist climb cord and
grapple, palm laser torch, laser finger (1D4 M.D., 300 ft), tool hand,
built-in loudspeaker, cyber-shield, shoulder weapon mounts, cyborg jet pack.

Officer: fundamentally the same, except four MOS skills (+15% each), five
other skills instead of three, and Hand to Hand: Martial Arts (or Assassin if
anarchist or evil).

The related-skill list prints "except Power Armor and Robot vehicles" on the
Pilot Related line; it is not enforced by the sheet. Secondary skills start at
level 2 (two each at levels 2, 4, 8 and 12). The save vs Horror Factor is +2
at level 1 and again at levels 3, 6, 9 and 12, as printed.
